      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope:**\n*   This CL is reported as `Size: L (+774, -0)`. Per `go/small-cls`, CLs of this size are too large to review effectively as a single atomic unit and must be split.\n*   **Proposed Split Plan:**\n    *   **CL 1:** Add the base `RtsUsbDevice` class structure and USB initialization/detachment/cleanup logic.\n    *   **CL 2:** Implement the core DFU download protocol and polling logic within `RtsUsbDevice`.\n    *   **CL 3:** Add the command-line utility entry point (`main`, `parse_args`, `read_file`) and build system integration.\n\n**Functionality \u0026 Robustness:**\n*   **Short Read Bug:** The `dfu_poll_idle` method checks `ret \u003c 0` for `libusb_control_transfer`, but a short read (e.g., `ret \u003d\u003d 0`) would lead to accessing uninitialized memory when reading the response bytes.\n*   **Previous Feedback Addressed:** The unused CRC32 dead code was removed, driver detachment was relocated to the correct DFU interface claim, and the fixed sleep was replaced with a polling wait loop.\n\n**Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:**\n*   The code uses C headers (`\u003cstdio.h\u003e`, `\u003cstdint.h\u003e`) instead of their C++ equivalents (`\u003ccstdio\u003e`, `\u003ccstdint\u003e`).\n*   Constants are defined using preprocessor `#define` macros instead of type-safe `constexpr` values.\n*   Output parameters (e.g., `cfg` in `parse_args`) use pointers rather than idiomatic C++ non-const references, and include unnecessary `struct` keywords.\n\n**Commit Message:**\n*   The commit message accurately describes the changes but is missing the mandatory `TEST\u003d` footer required for Chromium OS CLs. (See inline comment on `/COMMIT_MSG`).\n\n**Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:**\n*   While this is a hardware-interacting host tool, the pure logic components (such as argument parsing and file reading) have no automated test coverage. When splitting this CL, please add a small suite of unit tests for these pure helpers to ensure regressions are caught.\n\nPlease address the issues above and split the CL into a stacked series.\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl7911746_00cd36aa-3393-4c85-952b-07d647e59cb8.pb)",
