      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] `libusb_control_transfer` returns the number of bytes transferred on success. If the device returns a short packet, `ret` will be `\u003e\u003d 0` but less than `sizeof(response)` (6 bytes), which means accessing `response[1]` through `response[4]` below will read uninitialized memory.\n\nCheck for a short read as well:\n```cpp\n\t\tuint8_t response[6];\n\t\tint ret \u003d libusb_control_transfer(\n\t\t\tdev_handle_, BMREQ_D2H_CLS_IF, DFU_GETSTATUS, 0,\n\t\t\tstatic_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(dfu_interface_), response,\n\t\t\tsizeof(response), USB_DFU_TIMEOUT_MS);\n\n\t\tif (ret \u003c 6) {\n\t\t\tfprintf(stderr, \"DFU_GETSTATUS failed: %s\\n\",\n\t\t\t\tret \u003c 0 ? libusb_error_name(ret) : \"short read\");\n\t\t\treturn false;\n\t\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl7911746_00cd36aa-3393-4c85-952b-07d647e59cb8.pb)",
